# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: revendor-check-versions-exceptions — the accepted-exceptions mechanism must go back upstream to informatimago/rules
#+STATUS: WIP
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: infra
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-09-26

* Context

=scripts/check-versions.sh= is a VENDORED copy of the shared audit from
[[https://gitlab.com/informatimago/rules][informatimago/rules]]
(=scripts/check-versions.sh= there). AGENTS.md § /Build, install and release
structure/ states the rule: *fix it there, then re-vendor.*

clautolisp 2.2.109 broke that order, knowingly. It added an
ACCEPTED-EXCEPTIONS mechanism to the vendored copy while closing
=version-invariants-broken-by-shakedown-release=: the audit had been failing
on every run for the two documented 1.8-shakedown lines, which is precisely
how a gate stops being read. The session that made the change was sandboxed to
this repository's worktree and could not commit to another repository, so the
fix landed here first.

* What must go upstream

1. =scripts/check-versions.sh= — the exceptions block (=exception_match=, the
   =bad()= wrapper, the stale sweep, the summary counters) and the two header
   paragraphs describing it. The mechanism is project-INDEPENDENT; only the
   list it reads is project-local, so it belongs in the shared copy. Take the
   file as-is from clautolisp master; it is a strict superset of the current
   upstream copy (no other behaviour changed).
2. =version-rules.md= — a short § under § 6 describing the mechanism, so other
   projects know the facility exists and what it refuses:
   - one exception per line: =<glob matched against the check's message> # why=;
   - a reason is REQUIRED (an exception nobody can justify is not one);
   - an exception matching NOTHING fails as =stale=, so the list shrinks when
     the situation is resolved and cannot grow into a blanket;
   - only an IMMUTABLE PUBLISHED REF qualifies — anything still fixable gets
     fixed, not declared;
   - default list =scripts/version-audit-exceptions.txt=, overridable with
     =$VERSION_AUDIT_EXCEPTIONS=.
3. Once upstream carries it, re-vendor into this repository (the file should
   then be byte-identical again) and drop this issue.

* Measured 2026-09-27 — the round trip is smaller than it reads, and one claim above is wrong

The upstream clone is at =~/src/public/rules= (readable from here), so the diff
is no longer a guess:

| file                       | added | modified | removed |
|----------------------------+-------+----------+---------|
| =scripts/check-versions.sh=  |   106 |        4 |       0 |

*One file*, and upstream's copy has an mtime of 2026-07-26 — so there is no
upstream divergence to merge: re-vendoring is a whole-file copy, in the
direction OUR copy → upstream, then back.

*The claim "it is a strict superset ... (no other behaviour changed)" is not
literally true and should not be relied on for a blind copy.* Four lines are
MODIFIED rather than added, and a reviewer should look at exactly those:

1. the header comment "Project-independent: it reads nothing but git refs" —
   reworded, because the script now reads an exceptions FILE as well as git
   refs, and that sentence would otherwise be false upstream too;
2. =bad()= — re-implemented as the wrapper that consults =exception_match=
   before counting a violation. This is the mechanism;
3. the success =printf= — now names how many accepted exceptions were applied,
   so a green run states its own caveats;
4. the failure =printf= — same reason, on the other branch.

Behaviourally it IS a superset (nothing was taken away), which is presumably
what the sentence meant. But the review is four lines, not one hundred and
ten, and saying so is the difference between a five-minute round trip and a
re-reading of the whole file.

*Why this session still cannot do it, verified rather than assumed.* Git
operations against =~/src/public/rules= are refused outright — the worktree
isolation rejects any git invocation whose target is a different checkout, and
a plain =cd= into it before =git= is refused too. So the constraint that
created this ticket in 2.2.109 is unchanged, and the remaining work is
someone-with-access running a copy and reviewing four lines.

* Verification

Upstream and vendored copies identical (=diff=), and =make check-versions=
still exits 0 here with the two accepted exceptions, 1 on a stale or
reason-less exception, and 1 on any unlisted violation. Those four cases were
checked when the mechanism landed; re-check them after the round trip, since
the value of this change is entirely in the cases that still FAIL.

* Note

Filed per AGENTS.md's "a bug or a follow-up found while doing something else
gets its own ticket" rule, rather than left as a comment in the closed issue.

* Upstream MR opened 2026-10-03 -- informatimago/rules!1

Git against ~/src/public/rules is still refused in this session, but the
GitLab API is not git: branch =accepted-exceptions= on informatimago/rules
(commit 5ebda834) carries scripts/check-versions.sh -- byte-identical to
this repository's copy (cmp) -- and version-rules.md § 6.1, "Accepted
exceptions", plus the § 6 sentence "reads nothing but git refs" amended.
MR: https://gitlab.com/informatimago/rules/-/merge_requests/1 (review the
four modified lines named above). make check-versions here: 0, two
accepted exceptions.

LEFT: pjb merges !1. Re-vendoring is then a no-op (identical already);
close this ticket on the merge.
